    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2QaT2HKFAS5qjaYzA8ioqLq)_\n\n## Summary\n\n- Relaunched Emacs often opens a small frame that AeroSpace leaves floating.\n- Likely cause: `sp-frame.el` sets `(undecorated . t)` in `default-frame-alist`, and AeroSpace may not treat undecorated windows as standard.\n- Adds an `[[on-window-detected]]` rule for `org.gnu.Emacs` with `layout tiling`.\n- Only the first matching rule runs, so a rule before it keeps the `quick-capture` popup floating.\n- No Emacs frame settings changed.\n- Documented in `aerospace.org`, section \"Emacs frames tile\".\n- No CHANGELOG edit (the nightly tidy owns it; this belongs in the global one).\n\n## Not verified\n\n- The Mac was not reachable from the cloud session, so the app id `org.gnu.Emacs` and the floating layout were not checked on the device.\n- First check: `aerospace list-windows --all --format '%{app-bundle-id} %{window-layout} %{window-title}'`.\n- If the id differs, change it in both rules.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] `aerospace reload-config` shows no error\n- [ ] Quit and relaunch Emacs several times: the first frame tiles to the side\n- [x] New frame with `C-x 5 2` tiles\n- [ ] vulpea-ui view frame (`M-o v`) tiles\n- [ ] Quick capture frame stays floating\n- [ ] Other apps are not affected\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCdojFnPgFvFm1dj4R)_",
